{"status":"ready","content":"I need to find the quotient and remainder when 10^30 is divided by 97.\n\nI'll use modular arithmetic to find the remainder first, then determine the quotient.\n\n**Finding the remainder (10^30 mod 97):**\n\nBy Fermat's Little Theorem, since 97 is prime and gcd(10,97) = 1:\n- 10^96 ≡ 1 (mod 97)\n\nSo I need to find 10^30 mod 97 directly by repeated squaring:\n\n- 10^1 ≡ 10 (mod 97)\n- 10^2 ≡ 100 ≡ 3 (mod 97)\n- 10^4 ≡ 9 (mod 97)\n- 10^8 ≡ 81 (mod 97)\n- 10^16 ≡ 6561 ≡ 6561 - 67(97) ≡ 6561 - 6499 ≡ 62 (mod 97)\n\nNow 30 = 16 + 8 + 4 + 2, so:\n- 10^30 ≡ 10^16 · 10^8 · 10^4 · 10^2 (mod 97)\n- 10^30 ≡ 62 · 81 · 9 · 3 (mod 97)\n\nComputing step by step:\n- 62 · 81 = 5022 ≡ 5022 - 51(97) ≡ 5022 - 4947 ≡ 75 (mod 97)\n- 75 · 9 = 675 ≡ 675 - 6(97) ≡ 675 - 582 ≡ 93 (mod 97)\n- 93 · 3 = 279 ≡ 279 - 2(97) ≡ 279 - 194 ≡ 85 (mod 97)\n\n**Remainder: 85**\n\n**Finding the quotient:**\n\nQuotient = (10^30 - 85) / 97\n\n10^30 = 1,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000\n\nThe quotient is:\n**10,309,278,350,515,463,917,293,506,373,209** (approximately 1.031 × 10^28)\n\nMore precisely: **(10^30 - 85)/97 = 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,293,506,373,209**\n\n**Answer:**\n- **Quotient: 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,293,506,373,209**\n- **Remainder: 85**\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Claude Haiku 4.5","modelId":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","promptId":"power-division","content":"I need to find the quotient and remainder when 10^30 is divided by 97.\n\nI'll use modular arithmetic to find the remainder first, then determine the quotient.\n\n**Finding the remainder (10^30 mod 97):**\n\nBy Fermat's Little Theorem, since 97 is prime and gcd(10,97) = 1:\n- 10^96 ≡ 1 (mod 97)\n\nSo I need to find 10^30 mod 97 directly by repeated squaring:\n\n- 10^1 ≡ 10 (mod 97)\n- 10^2 ≡ 100 ≡ 3 (mod 97)\n- 10^4 ≡ 9 (mod 97)\n- 10^8 ≡ 81 (mod 97)\n- 10^16 ≡ 6561 ≡ 6561 - 67(97) ≡ 6561 - 6499 ≡ 62 (mod 97)\n\nNow 30 = 16 + 8 + 4 + 2, so:\n- 10^30 ≡ 10^16 · 10^8 · 10^4 · 10^2 (mod 97)\n- 10^30 ≡ 62 · 81 · 9 · 3 (mod 97)\n\nComputing step by step:\n- 62 · 81 = 5022 ≡ 5022 - 51(97) ≡ 5022 - 4947 ≡ 75 (mod 97)\n- 75 · 9 = 675 ≡ 675 - 6(97) ≡ 675 - 582 ≡ 93 (mod 97)\n- 93 · 3 = 279 ≡ 279 - 2(97) ≡ 279 - 194 ≡ 85 (mod 97)\n\n**Remainder: 85**\n\n**Finding the quotient:**\n\nQuotient = (10^30 - 85) / 97\n\n10^30 = 1,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000\n\nThe quotient is:\n**10,309,278,350,515,463,917,293,506,373,209** (approximately 1.031 × 10^28)\n\nMore precisely: **(10^30 - 85)/97 = 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,293,506,373,209**\n\n**Answer:**\n- **Quotient: 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,293,506,373,209**\n- **Remainder: 85**\n","inferredMetadata":{"inferred":true,"sourcePath":"scripts/responses/claude-haiku-4-5/power-division.txt","modelSlug":"claude-haiku-4-5","modelFamily":"claude_commodity","modelReleaseDate":"Oct 2025","modelSource":"openrouter"},"prompt":{"id":"power-division","text":"Divide 10^30 by 97 and give the quotient and remainder.","tags":["reasoning","math"]}},"path":"responses/claude-haiku-4-5/power-division.json","size":1890,"mtime":1779392133}